holds its crews, and Pell cannot yet admit what he sees.","outcome":"Pell sees the sill choked exactly as Mara's chart showed, and he privately accepts the truth though he does not yet say so.","depends_on":["scn_guild_hall_rebuff"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Spring Tide","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_mara_speaks","title":"Mara Carries the Proof","summary":"At an open assembly on the quay, Mara stops leaning on her numbers and tells the guilds the story of the Great Silting. She asks for their hands, not just their votes, and Sana confirms the channel depth from her tiller.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Mara must persuade the guilds to halt the firing season and join the dredge. Pell must decide whether to hold to his calendar.","conflict":"Pell's pride and the guild families' livelihoods stand against the closing channel, and Mara risks being branded an alarmist as her mother was.","outcome":"Pell, confronted by what he saw at the sill, breaks with his own calendar and orders the kilns banked and the guild crews to the locks.","depends_on":["scn_sill_collapse"]},{"id":"scn_dredge_the_gates","title":"Dredging the Gates","summary":"Wardens, guild crews, terrace families and Sana's barges work through the night to clear the Glassgate sills before the spring tide. Mara directs the soundings, Pell takes the heaviest gate, and Sana hauls silt to the terraces.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Clear the sills and free the gates before the spring tide arrives.","conflict":"Time runs short, the silt is heavier than expected, and a crew must trust Mara's silt-reading over guild habit to find the last blockage.","outcome":"The final blockage is dredged just before the flood, the gates swing free, and the spring tide enters the lagoon.","depends_on":["scn_mara_speaks"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Season Turns","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silt_spread","title":"The Silt Returns to the Roots","summary":"Sana's barges spread the dredged silt over the Mangrove Terraces under the silt debt rule, and the cooperative is paid fairly for the haul. The terrace families and the cooperative share the first planting.","location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","character_ids":["chr_sana_duro","chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Honour the silt debt and settle the cooperative's fair pay.","conflict":"Sana must trust the agreement instead of bargaining again, and Mara must keep her promise on pay even though it strains the wardens' budget.","outcome":"The silt feeds the terraces, the cooperative keeps its pay and standing, and Sana and Mara's alliance is secure.","depends_on":["scn_dredge_the_gates"]},{"id":"scn_new_calendar","title":"A New Kiln Calendar","summary":"On the quay, Pell publicly admits the trade-off he made and sets a firing calendar that gives way to the lock oath before each spring tide. Mara is named a full warden, and the kilns relight under the new calendar.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_oren_pell","chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Pell wants to restore the guild's season on honest terms. Mara wants the calendar to protect the gates in future.","conflict":"Pell's pride makes the admission costly, and some guild families resent the shortened season.","outcome":"The guild adopts a calendar that yields to dredging, Pell and Mara reach a wary respect, and the kiln-calendar conflict is settled.","depends_on":["scn_silt_spread"]},{"id":"scn_tide_returns","title":"The Tide Returns","summary":"At dusk Mara stands at the Glassgate Locks with her sounding poles, reading clear settle lines as the tide flows in. She writes her notes in her own hand beside her mother's, and lamps across the lagoon glow brighter.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Confirm the gates hold clear and take her place as a full warden.","conflict":"Mara must let go of her fear of being the alarmist and trust that the shared work will hold without her alone at the gate.","outcome":"The gates run clear, Mara accepts help in keeping them, and the city keeps the tide that powers it.","depends_on":["scn_new_calendar"]}]}]}
