{"world_id":"wld_tidal_conservatories","title":"The Glass Tide","logline":"When junior tide-warden Mara Ilek finds the Glassgate Locks silting shut weeks ahead of schedule, she must overcome the proud Glassblower Guild master Oren Pell and win allies among the lagoon's cooperatives to halt the firing season and dredge the gates before the spring tide, or the city loses the tide that powers it.","theme":"Proof persuades only when it is shared and shouldered together.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Early Silt","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_sounding_poles","title":"The Sounding Poles","summary":"At dawn Mara reads the settle lines on her sounding poles at the Glassgate Locks and finds the sills choked far beyond the survey tables. She copies the numbers in her mother's hand and realises the spring tide is at risk.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Confirm that the lock sills are silting weeks ahead of the survey.","conflict":"Her silt-reading shows a pace that contradicts the official tide tables, and she fears being dismissed as an alarmist like her mother.","outcome":"Mara confirms the early silting and resolves to get the gates dredged before the spring tide, bound by the lock oath."},{"id":"scn_apprentice_work","title":"Apprentice Work","summary":"Mara carries her soundings to Bellmaker's Quay and presents them to Oren Pell. Pell, who has read the same tables, dismisses them as apprentice work and refuses to shorten the firing season.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Mara wants the guild to halt the firing season so the gates can be shut and dredged. Pell wants to keep the locks open through the full season.","conflict":"Mara assumes her numbers will persuade by themselves, while Pell cannot admit a trade-off and publicly rejects a junior warden's evidence.","outcome":"Pell refuses and the guild calendar stands, leaving Mara without authority or allies and with the kiln-calendar conflict now open.","depends_on":["scn_sounding_poles"]},{"id":"scn_barge_bargain","title":"The Barge Bargain","summary":"Mara seeks out Sana Duro in the Algae Fields and hires her barge to sound the gate channels. Sana bargains hard and names her price: a say in who owns the dredged silt.","location_id":"loc_algae_fields","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Mara needs channel soundings beyond what her poles can reach. Sana needs the dredging contract without giving up the cooperative's silt rights.","conflict":"Sana distrusts the wardens' charter and bargains when she should listen, while Mara cannot promise terrace silt that belongs to the commons.","outcome":"They agree to a cautious partnership: Sana will sound the channels now, and the silt question is deferred.","depends_on":["scn_apprentice_work"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"The Channels Fill","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_channel_soundings","title":"Soundings in the Fog","summary":"Sana's barge and Mara sound the gate channels in fog. Sana feels the depth through her tiller and finds the main channel shallowing faster than Mara's poles suggested.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Map how badly the channels are silting before the spring tide.","conflict":"Fog and shifting silt make soundings unreliable, and Sana's channel-reading disagrees with Mara's precise figures until they reconcile the two methods.","outcome":"They produce a combined chart showing the channel could close days before the spring tide, stronger evidence than Mara had alone.","depends_on":["scn_barge_bargain"]},{"id":"scn_terrace_silt","title":"What the Terraces Remember","summary":"Mara takes the chart to the Mangrove Terraces, where families recall the Great Silting and the hunger it caused. Sana presses the silt-rights question while the terrace families weigh in.","location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Win the terraces' backing for a dredge and settle where the dredged silt will go.","conflict":"Sana demands the cooperative keep its silt, but the silt debt rule requires it to be spread on the terraces within a season, and Mara fails to listen to Sana's worry about fair pay.","outcome":"The terrace families pledge labour and agree the silt will be spread on the terraces while the cooperative is paid for hauling, binding Sana to Mara's cause.","depends_on":["scn_channel_soundings"]},{"id":"scn_guild_hall_rebuff","title":"The Guild Hall Rebuff","summary":"Mara brings the combined chart and the terrace pledges before the guild masters. Pell, knowing the tables are right, attacks her figures and her mother's reputation, and Mara falters, afraid of sounding like an alarmist.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Mara wants the guilds to vote to halt the firing season. Pell wants to keep the season intact. Sana wants her evidence and her barge heard.","conflict":"Mara's flaw leaves her relying on numbers alone, and Pell's pride keeps him from conceding the trade-off he privately sees.","outcome":"The guild votes to keep firing, but Sana publicly stakes her barge on the wardens' evidence and the vote is only narrowly won.","depends_on":["scn_terrace_silt","scn_apprentice_work"]},{"id":"scn_sill_collapse","title":"The Sill Closes","summary":"A tide surge drives silt into the main sill and one gate jams. Mara and her warden crew cannot clear it alone, and the guild's kilns, drawing on lagoon gas, are visibly dimming as the flow falters.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Mara must clear the jammed gate under the lock oath. Pell comes to see the damage for himself and still wants to protect the season.","conflict":"The wardens are too few to dredge while the guild's own calendar withholds its crews, and Pell cannot yet admit what he sees.","outcome":"Pell sees the sill choked exactly as Mara's chart showed, and he privately accepts the truth though he does not yet say so.","depends_on":["scn_guild_hall_rebuff"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Spring Tide","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_mara_speaks","title":"Mara Carries the Proof","summary":"At an open assembly on the quay, Mara stops leaning on her numbers and tells the guilds the story of the Great Silting. She asks for their hands, not just their votes, and Sana confirms the channel depth from her tiller.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Mara must persuade the guilds to halt the firing season and join the dredge. Pell must decide whether to hold to his calendar.","conflict":"Pell's pride and the guild families' livelihoods stand against the closing channel, and Mara risks being branded an alarmist as her mother was.","outcome":"Pell, confronted by what he saw at the sill, breaks with his own calendar and orders the kilns banked and the guild crews to the locks.","depends_on":["scn_sill_collapse"]},{"id":"scn_dredge_the_gates","title":"Dredging the Gates","summary":"Wardens, guild crews, terrace families and Sana's barges work through the night to clear the Glassgate sills before the spring tide. Mara directs the soundings, Pell takes the heaviest gate, and Sana hauls silt to the terraces.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Clear the sills and free the gates before the spring tide arrives.","conflict":"Time runs short, the silt is heavier than expected, and a crew must trust Mara's silt-reading over guild habit to find the last blockage.","outcome":"The final blockage is dredged just before the flood, the gates swing free, and the spring tide enters the lagoon.","depends_on":["scn_mara_speaks"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Season Turns","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silt_spread","title":"The Silt Returns to the Roots","summary":"Sana's barges spread the dredged silt over the Mangrove Terraces under the silt debt rule, and the cooperative is paid fairly for the haul. The terrace families and the cooperative share the first planting.","location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","character_ids":["chr_sana_duro","chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Honour the silt debt and settle the cooperative's fair pay.","conflict":"Sana must trust the agreement instead of bargaining again, and Mara must keep her promise on pay even though it strains the wardens' budget.","outcome":"The silt feeds the terraces, the cooperative keeps its pay and standing, and Sana and Mara's alliance is secure.","depends_on":["scn_dredge_the_gates"]},{"id":"scn_new_calendar","title":"A New Kiln Calendar","summary":"On the quay, Pell publicly admits the trade-off he made and sets a firing calendar that gives way to the lock oath before each spring tide. Mara is named a full warden, and the kilns relight under the new calendar.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_oren_pell","chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Pell wants to restore the guild's season on honest terms. Mara wants the calendar to protect the gates in future.","conflict":"Pell's pride makes the admission costly, and some guild families resent the shortened season.","outcome":"The guild adopts a calendar that yields to dredging, Pell and Mara reach a wary respect, and the kiln-calendar conflict is settled.","depends_on":["scn_silt_spread"]},{"id":"scn_tide_returns","title":"The Tide Returns","summary":"At dusk Mara stands at the Glassgate Locks with her sounding poles, reading clear settle lines as the tide flows in. She writes her notes in her own hand beside her mother's, and lamps across the lagoon glow brighter.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Confirm the gates hold clear and take her place as a full warden.","conflict":"Mara must let go of her fear of being the alarmist and trust that the shared work will hold without her alone at the gate.","outcome":"The gates run clear, Mara accepts help in keeping them, and the city keeps the tide that powers it.","depends_on":["scn_new_calendar"]}]}]}
