warning","title":"The Edge of the Wells","summary":"Itho visits the Erasure Wells to understand what awaits the soul. He sees accounts that could not be balanced dissolving into the dark shafts. The weighing is called for the next bell.","location_id":"loc_erasure_wells","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Learn how little time remains and what failure costs.","conflict":"Nothing dissolved at the Wells can be undone, because the dead cannot return to life and only accounts move. Itho's trust in ink fails him when no one will listen to a warning.","outcome":"Itho resolves to confront the weighing itself, and to bring Hemo back with the proof he cannot yet seal.","depends_on":["scn_scribe_key"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Weighing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hemo_chooses","title":"The Lamp or the Page","summary":"Itho presses Hemo to come to the Hall of Scales. Hemo, by his index and without reading a sealed page, can swear to where the matching entry sits and that it contradicts the ledger. Doing so risks his lamp.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Win the lamplighter's key, the third seal.","conflict":"Procedure offers Hemo a place to hide and Dame Ors's threat still stands. Itho must trust a person rather than ink.","outcome":"Hemo gives his word, takes up his lamp and agrees to testify without reading a sealed page. Itho now needs only the weigher's key.","depends_on":["scn_ors_threat","scn_wells_warning"]},{"id":"scn_the_weighing","title":"The Soul on the Scales","summary":"At the Hall of Scales the soul is brought to be weighed. Itho and Hemo present the proof as the scales are set. Dame Ors, who can detect a doctored balance, must either weigh the soul as written or seal the correction.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Itho and Hemo want the weigher's seal before the weighing. Dame Ors wants to weigh as written and quash the audit.","conflict":"Her seal would sit beside the error, and she calls her concealment mercy. Hemo's testimony puts his lamp on the line, and Itho must hold his temper without trusting ink alone.","outcome":"Dame Ors reads the soul's true weight and sees that the scales confirm the correction. Unable to deceive herself, she chooses the scales' honesty and gives the weigher's key. All three keys are turned.","depends_on":["scn_scribe_key","scn_hemo_chooses","scn_ors_threat"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Corrected Count","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_correction_sealed","title":"Sealed by Three Hands","summary":"The three seals are set on the corrected ledger entry. The soul is weighed against the right column and allowed to rest. Dame Ors is exposed by her own certification.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Seal the correction under the three-key rule so it stands.","conflict":"Dame Ors faces the cost of her admission before the collegium. Hemo's lamp hangs on whether his testimony counts as reading a sealed page, and Itho's seniors watch for blame.","outcome":"The correction stands, and the soul is weighed against what it actually did. The cost to Dame Ors and Hemo is still undecided.","depends_on":["scn_the_weighing"]},{"id":"scn_hemo_keeps_lamp","title":"The Lamp Kept","summary":"In the Lamp Archive, the lamplighters judge that Hemo only spoke an index position and never read a sealed page. He keeps his lamp and his post. The archive agrees to open ledgers for future audits with a weigher's warrant.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_hemo_lux","chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Settle whether Hemo broke his lamp oath.","conflict":"The oath's letter is strict and Hemo's old habit is to hide behind it. He must now stand in the open to defend what he did.","outcome":"Hemo keeps his lamp. The dispute over sealed ledgers eases without a rule being