{"world_id":"wld_underworld_ledger","title":"The Last Audit","logline":"A junior scribe who spots a mortal soul tallied to the wrong ledger column must win three unwilling seals, from a scribe, a weigher and a lamplighter, before a proud senior weigher weighs the soul as written and sends it to the Erasure Wells.","theme":"A correction is only ink until unwilling hands agree to seal it.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Dropped Letter","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_miscast_found","title":"The Column That Does Not Add","summary":"Copying accounts in the Counting Halls, Itho Pel's fault-sight catches a mortal soul entered in the wrong ledger column. By the rules, the soul will be weighed against a miscast ledger and sent to the Erasure Wells.","location_id":"loc_counting_halls","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Confirm that the entry is miscast and learn when the soul will be weighed.","conflict":"His seniors in the Order of Scribes wave off the error. Itho must accuse the offices that feed him, and he trusts ink more than the people who might help.","outcome":"Itho confirms the miscast and learns the weighing is imminent. He decides to carry a correction up the counting-houses, and he knows it needs three keys."},{"id":"scn_gate_slip","title":"The Tally-Slip at the Gate","summary":"Itho goes to the Gate of Receipts to inspect the soul's surrendered tally-slip. The slip shows the original entry was sound, and that the column was altered after the Counting Halls transcribed it. The soul waits in the queue for weighing.","location_id":"loc_gate_of_receipts","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Find physical proof of where the entry went wrong.","conflict":"Gate clerks guard the slips and will not release one to a junior scribe, so Itho can only read it where it lies. His obstinacy makes him argue the point aloud and draws attention.","outcome":"Itho learns the weigher's certification came after the alteration. The proof implicates the weighers, and he needs a matching archive entry to make it stand.","depends_on":["scn_miscast_found"]},{"id":"scn_ors_certifies","title":"The Certification","summary":"Dame Ors reviews the harvest of tallies in the Hall of Scales and privately recognises that the column is wrong. She tells herself the error is small and resolves to weigh the soul as written to protect the weighers' infallibility.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Keep the collegium's record clean and weigh the soul as written.","conflict":"She knows the column is wrong. Her self-deceiving flaw makes her call the concealment mercy, and the miscast tallies are already rising and drawing blame.","outcome":"Dame Ors sets the weighing on the schedule and resolves to quash any audit. Itho now faces an opponent with the authority to bar him."}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Three Keys","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_scales_barred","title":"Barred from the Scales","summary":"Itho brings his proof to the Hall of Scales to petition a weigher's key. Dame Ors receives him with courtesy and refuses him, because the collegium bars junior scribes from the scales.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Itho wants a weigher to take his petition. Dame Ors wants him gone.","conflict":"Her authority and the collegium's rule shut him out. Itho's earnest bluntness about trusting ink over people costs him the goodwill of the other weighers.","outcome":"Itho is turned away. Dame Ors learns the audit exists and that Itho needs the Lamp Archive, so she moves to cut him off there.","depends_on":["scn_gate_slip","scn_ors_certifies"]},{"id":"scn_hemo_index","title":"The Index He Is Forbidden to Read","summary":"Itho seeks out Hemo Lux in the Lamp Archive. Hemo cannot read a sealed page without losing his lamp, but his index memory can place the matching ledger and its cross-references without opening it.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Itho wants the matching archive entry located. Hemo wants to help without breaking his oath.","conflict":"Hemo hides behind procedure. The lamplighters also refuse to open sealed ledgers for an audit without a weigher's warrant, which Itho cannot get.","outcome":"Hemo names the exact ledger and page where the matching entry lies, but will not open it without a warrant. Itho now knows what to prove and where.","depends_on":["scn_scales_barred"]},{"id":"scn_ors_threat","title":"A Threat to the Lamp","summary":"Dame Ors visits the Lamp Archive and warns Hemo that his lamp is forfeit if he assists the audit. She frames the threat as protecting him from ruin.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_dame_ors","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Dame Ors wants to quash the audit by isolating Itho from the archive.","conflict":"Hemo's oath shelters the fraud, and his fear of losing his lamp pushes him toward silence. Dame Ors must also avoid showing how much she fears the entry.","outcome":"Hemo is shaken and withdraws his help for the moment. Itho will have to find a warrant on his own, and Dame Ors has revealed her fear.","depends_on":["scn_hemo_index"]},{"id":"scn_scribe_key","title":"The Unwilling Scribe","summary":"Itho returns to the Counting Halls and asks a senior scribe of the Order to vouch for the correction as the first key. He offers the tally-slip proof and the page reference Hemo gave him.","location_id":"loc_counting_halls","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Secure the scribe's key, the first of the three seals.","conflict":"The senior scribes fear that vouching will admit that the scribes and weighers each caused the miscast harvest. Itho must accuse his own order to win it.","outcome":"After Itho shows the slip, the Order's seal is given grudgingly. The first key is won, and word travels up that the audit is real.","depends_on":["scn_gate_slip","scn_hemo_index"]},{"id":"scn_wells_warning","title":"The Edge of the Wells","summary":"Itho visits the Erasure Wells to understand what awaits the soul. He sees accounts that could not be balanced dissolving into the dark shafts. The weighing is called for the next bell.","location_id":"loc_erasure_wells","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Learn how little time remains and what failure costs.","conflict":"Nothing dissolved at the Wells can be undone, because the dead cannot return to life and only accounts move. Itho's trust in ink fails him when no one will listen to a warning.","outcome":"Itho resolves to confront the weighing itself, and to bring Hemo back with the proof he cannot yet seal.","depends_on":["scn_scribe_key"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Weighing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hemo_chooses","title":"The Lamp or the Page","summary":"Itho presses Hemo to come to the Hall of Scales. Hemo, by his index and without reading a sealed page, can swear to where the matching entry sits and that it contradicts the ledger. Doing so risks his lamp.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Win the lamplighter's key, the third seal.","conflict":"Procedure offers Hemo a place to hide and Dame Ors's threat still stands. Itho must trust a person rather than ink.","outcome":"Hemo gives his word, takes up his lamp and agrees to testify without reading a sealed page. Itho now needs only the weigher's key.","depends_on":["scn_ors_threat","scn_wells_warning"]},{"id":"scn_the_weighing","title":"The Soul on the Scales","summary":"At the Hall of Scales the soul is brought to be weighed. Itho and Hemo present the proof as the scales are set. Dame Ors, who can detect a doctored balance, must either weigh the soul as written or seal the correction.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Itho and Hemo want the weigher's seal before the weighing. Dame Ors wants to weigh as written and quash the audit.","conflict":"Her seal would sit beside the error, and she calls her concealment mercy. Hemo's testimony puts his lamp on the line, and Itho must hold his temper without trusting ink alone.","outcome":"Dame Ors reads the soul's true weight and sees that the scales confirm the correction. Unable to deceive herself, she chooses the scales' honesty and gives the weigher's key. All three keys are turned.","depends_on":["scn_scribe_key","scn_hemo_chooses","scn_ors_threat"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Corrected Count","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_correction_sealed","title":"Sealed by Three Hands","summary":"The three seals are set on the corrected ledger entry. The soul is weighed against the right column and allowed to rest. Dame Ors is exposed by her own certification.","location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors","chr_hemo_lux"],"goal":"Seal the correction under the three-key rule so it stands.","conflict":"Dame Ors faces the cost of her admission before the collegium. Hemo's lamp hangs on whether his testimony counts as reading a sealed page, and Itho's seniors watch for blame.","outcome":"The correction stands, and the soul is weighed against what it actually did. The cost to Dame Ors and Hemo is still undecided.","depends_on":["scn_the_weighing"]},{"id":"scn_hemo_keeps_lamp","title":"The Lamp Kept","summary":"In the Lamp Archive, the lamplighters judge that Hemo only spoke an index position and never read a sealed page. He keeps his lamp and his post. The archive agrees to open ledgers for future audits with a weigher's warrant.","location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","character_ids":["chr_hemo_lux","chr_itho_pel"],"goal":"Settle whether Hemo broke his lamp oath.","conflict":"The oath's letter is strict and Hemo's old habit is to hide behind it. He must now stand in the open to defend what he did.","outcome":"Hemo keeps his lamp. The dispute over sealed ledgers eases without a rule being broken.","depends_on":["scn_correction_sealed"]},{"id":"scn_new_column","title":"A New Entry in the Margin","summary":"Back in the Counting Halls, Itho copies the corrected account into the ledger. Dame Ors comes to witness it, her certification now corrected and her infallibility gone. Itho learns that a correction is only ink until three unwilling hands agree.","location_id":"loc_counting_halls","character_ids":["chr_itho_pel","chr_dame_ors"],"goal":"Itho wants the ledger set right and the miscast harvest audited. Dame Ors wants to face what she did.","conflict":"The scribes and weighers still blame each other's desks. Itho must keep trusting the people who sealed with him and not only the ink.","outcome":"The correction is entered and the audit of the harvest continues. Itho trusts the hands that sealed as well as the ink, and Dame Ors accepts the cost of choosing the scales' honesty over her own.","depends_on":["scn_correction_sealed","scn_hemo_keeps_lamp"]}]}]}
