{"world_id":"wld_bellwether","title":"The Ninth Bell","logline":"When Elsa Quill, a bell-founder's apprentice, hears an unmarked tenth ring in the storm-bells, she must trace it to its caster before Warden Hale's silence writ stills the wall and leaves Bellwether defenceless against the name-stealing Chiming.","theme":"A mark is only a signature, and signatures can be forged.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Unmarked Ring","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_foundry_flaw","title":"A Ring Without a Mark","summary":"In the Founder Row foundry, Elsa listens to the wall's bells carried on the evening wind and hears a tenth tone that matches no founder's mark. She reads it as a casting no collegium hand made.","location_id":"loc_founder_row","character_ids":["chr_elsa_quill"],"goal":"Identify whose mark the strange ring carries.","conflict":"Her ring-sight finds no founder's mark in it, which contradicts everything she was taught about how bells are traced.","outcome":"Elsa resolves to prove the tenth ring was cast by a human hand and to clear the collegium, and she heads for the wall to hear it at its source."},{"id":"scn_belfry_listening","title":"Listening at the Belfry","summary":"Elsa climbs the Sea-Wall Belfry at dusk and hears the pattern properly. The tenth ring falls in the gap between the ninth bell and the fog, and its flaw is fresh, a recent casting.","location_id":"loc_sea_wall","character_ids":["chr_elsa_quill"],"goal":"Confirm the tenth ring is a real bell and judge how recently it was cast.","conflict":"Fog is gathering and speaking aloud risks her name, so she must work in silence, and the unmarked ring is masked by the nine true bells.","outcome":"Elsa learns the casting is new and made by someone who knew founder craft. She now has a reason to suspect a trained hand and needs a lead on the caster.","depends_on":["scn_foundry_flaw"]},{"id":"scn_writ_read","title":"The Silence Writ","summary":"On Bailiff's Stairs, Warden Hale has the writ read ordering the bells silenced before the next fog, citing the unmarked tenth bell as proof the wall is corrupted. Elsa hears it and confronts him.","location_id":"loc_bailiffs_stairs","character_ids":["chr_warden_hale","chr_elsa_quill"],"goal":"Hale wants the writ confirmed and the wall stilled before the next fog, while Elsa wants it delayed.","conflict":"Hale moves writs through the court faster than anyone can answer them, and Elsa has no proof of the caster to set against him.","outcome":"The writ stands with a deadline of the next fog. Elsa leaves with a hard clock and Hale marks her as an obstacle.","depends_on":["scn_belfry_listening"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Names and Forgeries","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_fogmarket_approach","title":"The Fogmarket Opens","summary":"With the founders' registers offering nothing, Elsa follows a rumour into the Fogmarket, which has opened in thin fog, and finds Tallow, who admits he knows whom the tenth bell was cast for.","location_id":"loc_fogmarket","character_ids":["chr_elsa_quill","chr_tallow"],"goal":"Elsa wants the name of the tenth bell's caster, and Tallow wants a price and safe passage.","conflict":"Tallow prices everything, and his price is a name-token Elsa is sworn to protect, which her unbending craft-rule honesty makes hard to pay.","outcome":"Tallow agrees to sell a clue, not the name itself, and sets a meeting at the salt chapel, since he is nervous of his own name-debt.","depends_on":["scn_writ_read"]},{"id":"scn_salt_registry","title":"Names on Salt","summary":"At the Salt Chapel, Tallow shows Elsa a salt registry entry altered in a fresh hand. The ringer's name was written over, and the bell was cast against a registered name, not a founder's mark.","location_id":"loc_salt_chapel","character_ids":["chr_elsa_quill","chr_tallow"],"goal":"Elsa wants to read the evidence tying the bell to a caster, and Tallow wants to be paid and gone before the fog calls in his debt.","conflict":"The registry is forfeit to the fog if a name is erased, and Tallow fears being overheard, while Elsa's trust in marks makes her doubt a mark could be forged.","outcome":"Elsa learns the tenth bell was cast with a forged founder's mark, which breaks her faith in how marks prove makers and points to someone with watch access to the registry.","depends_on":["scn_fogmarket_approach"]},{"id":"scn_hale_pressure","title":"Hale Tightens the Writ","summary":"Hale learns Elsa has been asking about the registry. On Bailiff's Stairs he offers her a quiet bargain, to drop her search and keep the collegium unharmed, and when she refuses he moves the silencing date up.","location_id":"loc_bailiffs_stairs","character_ids":["chr_warden_hale","chr_elsa_quill"],"goal":"Hale wants Elsa to stand down, and Elsa wants time to prove the caster.","conflict":"Hale believes any means are justified to still the bells, and Elsa realises her craft rules have been turned into a weapon against her own people.","outcome":"The silencing is moved up to the coming night's fog, and Elsa now knows the watch is behind the forgery but lacks proof she can show.","depends_on":["scn_salt_registry"]},{"id":"scn_tallow_choice","title":"The Price of Honesty","summary":"At the Fogmarket, the watch and the founders both come for the ringer's name. Tallow, cornered, decides whether to sell the name to the highest bidder or to Elsa, and the fog thickens around his stall.","location_id":"loc_fogmarket","character_ids":["chr_tallow","chr_elsa_quill"],"goal":"Tallow wants safe passage from his debt, and Elsa wants the true name before the bells are stilled.","conflict":"Selling the name betrays the only client who paid fair, and everyone else would take it without paying.","outcome":"Tallow sells Elsa the truth cheap and keeps the name safe in his memory, and Elsa now holds the proof that the unmarked bell was cast at the watch's order. She must get it to the wall in time.","depends_on":["scn_hale_pressure"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Wall Rings","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_belfry_confrontation","title":"Confession at the Belfry","summary":"As fog rolls in, Hale arrives at the Sea-Wall Belfry with the watch to still the bells. Elsa uses her ring-sight to show that the tenth bell's flaw and forged mark come from the watch's casting, and the bells ring.","location_id":"loc_sea_wall","character_ids":["chr_elsa_quill","chr_warden_hale","chr_tallow"],"goal":"Hale wants the wall silenced, and Elsa wants to expose the forged tenth bell before the fog takes the parish.","conflict":"The writ gives Hale legal force, the fog is already stealing names, and Elsa's proof depends on a mark she once trusted completely.","outcome":"The unmarked bell tolls its own flaw, which Elsa reads aloud as the watch's casting, and Hale's confession is heard by the wardens. The writ is lost and the wall keeps ringing.","depends_on":["scn_tallow_choice"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"After the Fog","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_court_aftermath","title":"The Writ Withdrawn","summary":"On Bailiff's Stairs, the parish court withdraws the silence writ and holds Hale to answer for the treasonous tenth casting, as his own watch's bell stands as evidence against him.","location_id":"loc_bailiffs_stairs","character_ids":["chr_warden_hale","chr_elsa_quill"],"goal":"Elsa wants the writ formally withdrawn and the collegium cleared, and Hale wants to justify his ends.","conflict":"Hale insists the silence was necessary, and the watch must still answer for the extortion and the forged mark under the same laws.","outcome":"The writ is withdrawn, the collegium is cleared, and Hale is held to answer for his unrepentant treason.","depends_on":["scn_belfry_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_chapel_restoration","title":"Names Restored","summary":"Elsa and Tallow go to the Salt Chapel to correct the altered registry entry. Tallow buys back his own name, and Elsa accepts that a mark is a signature that can be forged.","location_id":"loc_salt_chapel","character_ids":["chr_elsa_quill","chr_tallow"],"goal":"Elsa wants the registry restored, and Tallow wants to settle his name-debt.","conflict":"The erased name is forfeit to the fog unless it is rewritten in time, and Elsa must face how much her faith in marks cost her.","outcome":"The registry is restored and Tallow's name is his again. Elsa carries a new rule into her craft, to check the hand behind the mark as well as the mark itself.","depends_on":["scn_court_aftermath"]},{"id":"scn_foundry_return","title":"Nine Bells Remain","summary":"Back on Founder Row, Elsa reports to the collegium that the tenth bell is evidence and is to be struck down, and she begins training to read forgeries as well as flaws as the nine bells ring the next fog back.","location_id":"loc_founder_row","character_ids":["chr_elsa_quill"],"goal":"Elsa wants to carry her new understanding of marks into the collegium's practice.","conflict":"The founders are reluctant to admit their marks can be forged and the wall still carries the stain of the tenth bell.","outcome":"The collegium adopts Elsa's check on marks and the nine bells ring the fog back, with the wall restored and her arc complete.","depends_on":["scn_chapel_restoration"]}]}]}
