air remembers the taste of each tea that sealed a bargain, and that the Ninth Stall's old recipe may carry the claim. Poppy brews her grandmother's blend for her.","location_id":"loc_wishing_barn","character_ids":["chr_mabel_thorn","chr_poppy_wren"],"goal":"Poppy wants to learn how to make the fair's memory carry her claim, and Mabel wants to teach without breaking her neutral role.","conflict":"Mabel lets the rules do her kindness and hints rather than speaks. Poppy's doubt makes her think the hints are refusals.","outcome":"Poppy learns the stall's old recipe must be served and recognised to prove descent. She also learns that an unkept favour is what lost the stall, and that she must find who it was owed to.","depends_on":["scn_damson_courts_the_round"]},{"id":"scn_carter_secrets","title":"The Carters' Closed Wains","summary":"Poppy goes among the Carter Kin on Leap Lane to find the ledger Damson read. She offers a trade of tea and a small favour for a look at the lane's secrets.","location_id":"loc_leap_lane","character_ids":["chr_poppy_wren","chr_damson_grey"],"goal":"Poppy wants to see the old ledger and learn whom the forfeited favour was owed to.","conflict":"Damson offers a bargain: she may see the ledger if she gives up the claim. He means it as a settling and tells himself it is fair. Poppy is tempted by certainty and nearly accepts.","outcome":"Poppy refuses, and as she leaves she glimpses a page naming the forfeited favour. She now knows it was owed to the Carter Kin and that Damson knows the claim is real.","depends_on":["scn_mabel_lessons_in_memory"]},{"id":"scn_the_bargain_contest","title":"The Contest of Cups","summary":"The Round holds a tea contest to settle whether to hear the claim before the sale. Poppy and Damson each serve a cup, and the Round judges by taste and truth.","location_id":"loc_kettle_commons","character_ids":["chr_poppy_wren","chr_damson_grey","chr_mabel_thorn"],"goal":"Poppy wants the Round to agree to hear her claim before the 