lause to stall her. Poppy must speak her claim plainly and without apology, and Mabel's tag will only count if Mabel reads it aloud against the carters' resentment.","outcome":"Poppy speaks without apologising. Mabel reads the old tag aloud, and the fair remembers with her. The cup is accepted and the favour is kept before the third bell, so the lease passes to Poppy's family and Damson's sale fails."}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Fair Remembers","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_damson_reads_back","title":"The Lease Reads Back","summary":"Damson reads the lease and finds a clause that names the carters' own part in the forfeiture. He settles it by bargain with the Tallykeepers: his factor's share is recorded as a favour owed to Poppy's stall, to be paid in trade.","location_id":"loc_wishing_barn","character_ids":["chr_damson_grey","chr_mabel_thorn","chr_poppy_wren"],"goal":"Damson wants a fair settlement that gives him some share. The Tallykeepers want the debt properly recorded.","conflict":"Damson must admit he knew the claim was real. Mabel records it plainly, and the carters resent a tag read aloud. Poppy must decide whether to accept the bargain without apologising.","outcome":"A new tag is hung binding Damson to supply the Ninth Stall's trade and sharing its custom. The conflict ends by bargain and nobody is harmed.","depends_on":["scn_closing_day_claim"]},{"id":"scn_opening_the_ninth","title":"The Ninth Stall Opens","summary":"Poppy unshutters the Ninth Stall and serves the first cup to the stallholders and the Carter Kin. The lanes begin to fold as she stands behind her own counter.","location_id":"loc_ninth_stall","character_ids":["chr_poppy_wren","chr_mabel_thorn","chr_damson_grey"],"goal":"Poppy wants to open the stall and serve her family's tea before the fair folds its lanes.","conflict":"The lanes are folding and there is little time. Poppy has to receive thanks and the fair's judgment without apologising for taking her place."