ous Host","summary":"Deva visits the Pepper Warehouses to check the bonded cargo manifests against the filing. Suleiman Qadir receives her warmly and offers a gift. She declines it, aware that an unregistered gift is a bribe under the gift register rule.","location_id":"loc_pepper_warehouses","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir"],"goal":"Deva wants the manifest dates to compare with the ledger, and Qadir wants to learn how far her audit will go.","conflict":"Qadir's courtesy hides pressure, and Deva's belief that the ledger cannot be wrong makes her reluctant to suspect the filing itself.","outcome":"Deva takes the manifest dates, and Qadir learns that she can read ink and begins to plan against her.","depends_on":["scn_envoy_house_quarrel"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"The Ink and the Gifts","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_ledger_audit","title":"The Audit by Lamplight","summary":"Deva recites her copied entries from memory and compares them with the ledger. The disputed entry matches the hand of no clerk, yet the ledger's order still seems to support it, which shakes her faith in the book.","location_id":"loc_harbour_office","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai"],"goal":"Deva wants to prove the disputed entry was written out of order.","conflict":"Her certainty that the ledger is never wrong makes her doubt her own findings, and senior slot-keepers obstruct the audit.","outcome":"She concludes that the entry was written later than its date and that someone inside the office allowed it, which implicates the court that raised her.","depends_on":["scn_qadir_receives_her"]},{"id":"scn_gift_register","title":"The Gift Register","summary":"Deva checks the gift register against the unregistered gifts found in the warehouses. Qadir arrives to invoke the court's authority, and a slot-keeper warns her that pressing the matter could cost her the office.","location_id":"loc_harbour_office","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir"],"goal":"Deva wants proof that the gifts bought the pre-dated filing, and Qadir wants to keep his slot until the monsoon is declared.","conflict":"Qadir's gifts have implicated the slot-keepers, so any accusation endangers Deva and the office that raised her.","outcome":"Deva finds the register silent on the gifts and realises that ink alone will not convict, and that she needs the sea's testimony of the hour.","depends_on":["scn_ledger_audit"]},{"id":"scn_amara_at_the_ghat","title":"The Pilot Ghat","summary":"Deva goes to the Pilot Ghat and asks Amara what she reads in the sea. Amara answers in omen-rite and will not be hurried, but agrees that her declaration can fix the true hour.","location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_amara"],"goal":"Deva wants Amara's reading to corroborate the true filing hour, and Amara wants to declare the wind honestly.","conflict":"Amara's rite must be taken on faith by the court, and every claimant wants her declaration delayed.","outcome":"Amara tells Deva the wind will turn within days and agrees to declare it in public rite, and Deva now has a deadline.","depends_on":["scn_gift_register"]},{"id":"scn_qadir_pressure","title":"The Price of a Record","summary":"Qadir tries to buy Deva off at the Pepper Warehouses with credit and promises of a post. When she refuses, he threatens the office that raised her and the court's trust in her.","location_id":"loc_pepper_warehouses","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir"],"goal":"Qadir wants Deva to let the audit end inconclusive, and Deva wants the full filing order.","conflict":"His forged filing saved his season and may cost his name, and the pressure on Deva grows with every refusal.","outcome":"Deva refuses, and Qadir turns to the gift-smoothed court to have the audit closed.","depends_on":["scn_amara_at_the_ghat"]},{"id":"scn_audit_closed","title":"The Audit Is Closed","summary":"At the Envoy House the three envoys, pressed by the court, agree to accept a compromise. Deva stands against it and tells the envoys that one claim was forged. Qadir's allies order her removed from the audit.","location_id":"loc_envoy_house","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir"],"goal":"Deva wants the envoys to hold off on the compromise, and Qadir wants it sealed before the wind turns.","conflict":"Without Amara's declaration or a registered gift record, Deva's word is the only evidence against a trusted factor.","outcome":"The audit is ordered closed, but the envoys are shaken, and Deva resolves to bring the proof to the public oath at the ghat.","depends_on":["scn_qadir_pressure"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Ghat Oath","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_wind_declared","title":"The Wind Is Declared","summary":"At the Pilot Ghat, Amara declares the monsoon turned in public rite. Deva sets her ink findings beside Amara's reading before the envoys and the court, and Qadir stands among them.","location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir","chr_amara"],"goal":"Deva wants to establish the true filing order, and Qadir wants to keep the first slot.","conflict":"Qadir argues that the ledger has never been wrong, and Deva's own belief in that is turned against her until she accepts that a ledger is only as honest as its writer.","outcome":"Amara's honest hour, set against the later-written entry, shows Qadir's filing was pre-dated, and the court must rule.","depends_on":["scn_audit_closed"]},{"id":"scn_qadir_oath","title":"The Oath over Pepper","summary":"Qadir is called to swear over pepper before the harbour court that his filing was true. Facing the choice between his slot and his name, he stops short of the oath.","location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir"],"goal":"Deva wants Qadir's forgery acknowledged under oath, and Qadir wants to keep the slot without losing his name.","conflict":"An oath over pepper is binding, so swearing falsely would end his name for good, while refusing ends his season.","outcome":"Qadir refuses the oath and gives up the first slot, and the earliest honest claim is left standing.","depends_on":["scn_wind_declared"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Season Sails","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_ledger_corrected","title":"The Ledger Corrected","summary":"Back in the Harbour Office, Deva enters the corrected filing order in the ledger. The court, shamed by the unregistered gifts, orders the gift register opened and the forged entry struck.","location_id":"loc_harbour_office","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai"],"goal":"Deva wants the ledger to record the true order before the fleet sails.","conflict":"The slot-keepers resist correcting the record because it exposes their own gifts, and Deva must write the correction against the office that raised her.","outcome":"The forged entry is struck and the first slot is awarded to the earliest honest claim, and Deva is no longer overlooked.","depends_on":["scn_qadir_oath"]},{"id":"scn_fleet_sails","title":"The Fleet Sails in Order","summary":"At the Pilot Ghat, Amara watches the fleet sail in the order the ledger now records. Qadir's cargo follows on the second wind, and he must rebuild his name with a smaller season.","location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir","chr_amara"],"goal":"Deva and Amara want to see the fleet leave in the right order, and Qadir wants to salvage what he can.","conflict":"Qadir's buyers are gone and his credit is strained, so he must face the cost of the choice he made at the oath.","outcome":"The fleet sails in the honest order, and Deva keeps the ledger with a newly earned wariness about whose hand writes in it.","depends_on":["scn_ledger_corrected"]}]}]}
