t a compromise. Deva stands against it and tells the envoys that one claim was forged. Qadir's allies order her removed from the audit.","location_id":"loc_envoy_house","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir"],"goal":"Deva wants the envoys to hold off on the compromise, and Qadir wants it sealed before the wind turns.","conflict":"Without Amara's declaration or a registered gift record, Deva's word is the only evidence against a trusted factor.","outcome":"The audit is ordered closed, but the envoys are shaken, and Deva resolves to bring the proof to the public oath at the ghat.","depends_on":["scn_qadir_pressure"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Ghat Oath","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_wind_declared","title":"The Wind Is Declared","summary":"At the Pilot Ghat, Amara declares the monsoon turned in public rite. Deva sets her ink findings beside Amara's reading before the envoys and the court, and Qadir stands among them.","location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir","chr_amara"],"goal":"Deva wants to establish the true filing order, and Qadir wants to keep the first slot.","conflict":"Qadir argues that the ledger has never been wrong, and Deva's own belief in that is turned against her until she accepts that a ledger is only as honest as its writer.","outcome":"Amara's honest hour, set against the later-written entry, shows Qadir's filing was pre-dated, and the court must rule.","depends_on":["scn_audit_closed"]},{"id":"scn_qadir_oath","title":"The Oath over Pepper","summary":"Qadir is called to swear over pepper before the harbour court that his filing was true. Facing the choice between his slot and his name, he stops short of the oath.","location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir"],"goal":"Deva wants Qadir's forgery acknowledged under oath, and Qadir wants to keep the slot without losing his name.","conflict":"An oath over pepper is binding, so swearing falsely would end his name for good, while refusing ends his season.","outcome":"Qadir refuses the oath and gives up the first slot, and the earliest honest claim is left standing.","depends_on":["scn_wind_declared"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Season Sails","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_ledger_corrected","title":"The Ledger Corrected","summary":"Back in the Harbour Office, Deva enters the corrected filing order in the ledger. The court, shamed by the unregistered gifts, orders the gift register opened and the forged entry struck.","location_id":"loc_harbour_office","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai"],"goal":"Deva wants the ledger to record the true order before the fleet sails.","conflict":"The slot-keepers resist correcting the record because it exposes their own gifts, and Deva must write the correction against the office that raised her.","outcome":"The forged entry is struck and the first slot is awarded to the earliest honest claim, and Deva is no longer overlooked.","depends_on":["scn_qadir_oath"]},{"id":"scn_fleet_sails","title":"The Fleet Sails in Order","summary":"At the Pilot Ghat, Amara watches the fleet sail in the order the ledger now records. Qadir's cargo follows on the second wind, and he must rebuild his name with a smaller season.","location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","character_ids":["chr_deva_anai","chr_suleiman_qadir","chr_amara"],"goal":"Deva and Amara want to see the fleet leave in the right order, and Qadir wants to salvage what he can.","conflict":"Qadir's buyers are gone and his credit is strained, so he must face the cost of the choice he made at the oath.","outcome":"The fleet sails in the honest order, and Deva keeps the ledger with a newly earned wariness about whose hand writes in it.","depends_on":["scn_ledger_corrected"]}]}]}
